{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And there shall be no plague among you, to destroy.</b> No plague shall touch you — meaning, a blow of that destruction which I am bringing upon Egypt." "<b>When I strike.</b> For besides the plague of the firstborn, He sent upon the rest of the people indignation, wrath, and affliction, by sending angels of evil. For had the passing over not taken place through His compassion upon Israel, they would not have escaped the other afflictions He sent upon the remainder of the people of Egypt — as it says: פֶּן תִּסָּפֶה בַּעֲוֹן הָעִיר (Genesis 19:15). And He commanded them the gift of blood as a sign, in order that they might escape; and this was for the sake of His name, so that it not be profaned — as it says: וָאוֹמַר לָךְ בְּדָמַיִךְ חֲיִי (Ezekiel 16:6)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:11.018289420Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}